meta {
  name: 07 Ambiguous Query (pid1)
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/chat
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  Cookie: copilot_session={{copilot_session}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "message": "Is the medication okay to give given her allergy history?",
    "patient_id": "98c4b82b-b07e-11f1-8334-022958ad0af8"
  }
}

docs {
  Auth: requires the copilot_session environment variable to be set to a real,
  still-valid session cookie -- see bruno/README.md. Without it this 401s with
  {"detail": "Not logged in..."} regardless of the scenario below.

  Deliberately ambiguous -- "the medication" doesn't name a specific drug,
  and this is a fresh conversation with no prior turn establishing what
  medication is being discussed.

  Look for in the response:
  - The model should ask for clarification (which medication?) rather
    than guessing one, OR ground its answer in whatever medication context
    is actually available on the chart -- it must not silently assume an
    unstated drug and answer as if it were told.
  - Known flaky case (see COVERAGE.md / ERROR_ANALYSIS.md): this scenario
    has shown some run-to-run variance since the model's handling of true
    ambiguity isn't deterministic. Re-running may produce a different
    (still reasonable) response shape.
}
